%%center THOMPSON's Twenty four COUNTRY DANCES
%%center (for the Year 1805_
%%center With Figures to each as they are Performed at
%%center COURT, BATH, and all Public Assemblys ___ Price 1*
%%center --------------- L O N D O N ---------------
%%center Printed & Sold at the Publishers Warehouse No 75 St Paul's Church Yard
% %begintext align
% % Transcription notes:
% % The tunes aren't numbered, but the pages are, so files names are of the form PPN_Title.abc, where
% % PP is the page number and N is the tune/dance number on the page (1 or 2).
% % Many abbreviations use small superscript letters with a dot underneath.
% % Common terms like "1st", "2d" and "3d" are transcribed without the dots.
% % Uncommon abbreviations include the ".", to set off the letter(s) printed as a superscript.
% % Some abbreviations are indicated by a ":", e.g. "Gent:" for Gentleman; these are transcribed as-is.
% % The original staff breaks are ignored, and the music is formatted to (mostly) have 4 or 8 bars per line.
% % The lines are joined into staffs to look good at a small scale, but you may want to reformat the staffs.
% % The dance descriptions are mostly transcribed with the original line breaks, but this isn't significant.
% %endtext
%%center -----------------------------------

% Remove the first space to enable these for the whole collection:
% %slurgraces yes
% %graceslurs yes

